<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Mexican Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1821">1821</a>–<a href="/years/1823">1823</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Mexican Empire was the monarchy established after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> won independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1821, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agustin-de-iturbide">Agustín de Iturbide</a> crowned as Emperor Agustín I in 1822. It briefly stretched from the northern frontier of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a>, whose provinces were annexed in 1822. Opposition led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-lopez-de-santa-anna">Antonio López de Santa Anna</a> forced Iturbide to abdicate in 1823, and Mexico became a federal republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-mexican-empire.jpg" alt="First Mexican Empire" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ludovicus Ferdinandus Can have elements by Sodacan and Heralder · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandera_del_Primer_Imperio_Mexicano.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
